              "answer_ending_700_chars": "*   The 6th face is the Flap.\n        *   The gap is 1 face wide.\n        *   The edges bounding the gap are the edge \"before\" the flap and the edge \"after\" the flap (which is edge x).\n        *   The edge \"after\" the flap is x.\n        *   The edge \"before\" the flap is the top edge of Tri 1 (Edge 3).\n        *   Wait, the flap is at the end of the strip.\n        *   The sequence is: [Edge 3] - Tri 1 - Tri 2 - Tri 3 - Tri 4 - Tri 5 - [Flap x].\n        *   When wrapped, Edge 3 meets Edge x.\n        *   This is the standard logic for strip nets. The start of the strip meets the end of the strip.\n        *   Start: Edge 3.\n        *   End: Edge x.\n        *   Therefore, **Edge 3 meets Edge x**.",
